quick_facts: 'Father of the Nuclear Navy'
quick_facts: USS Nautilus: first nuclear submarine (1954), reached North Pole 1958
quick_facts: 63 years of service — longest in U.S. Navy history
quick_facts: His safety program has run reactors without major release since the 1950s
